    {
        "text": "Though the conversation that follows is incredibly embarrassing, Sakiko follows the kind townsperson's instructions and successfully makes her way 'back'."
    },
    {
        "text": "Following the meandering path, she at last arrives at the door of what is allegedly her home. A white, strange building."
    },
    {
        "text": "The flowers and grass in the courtyard are well maintained. She can hear the flowerbeds' sprinklers quietly watering the plants around them. The chimney lets out puffs of smoke, as the master of the house prepares lunch."
    },
    {
        "text": "But she knows that this return is not to her real home."
    },
    {
        "text": "Her real home is in a faraway, unreachable place."
    },
    {
        "text": "Home. The first thing that comes to her mind is the Togawa family mansion, followed by the dusty, cramped little place her father rented that always smells of alcohol."
    },
    {
        "text": "She thinks about how hardworking her father once was."
    },
    {
        "text": "Alas, her real father is probably wandering the streets with a bottle of booze right now. He might even be uttering her name, though the sorry excuses he gives alongside are the furthest thing from 'sweet'."
    },
    {
        "text": "Right. That is Sakiko Togawa's reality."
    },
    {
        "text": "What she sees before her is a dream spun for her by Morpheus, and it doubles as a cage to imprison her."
    },
    {
